WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.060
The voter intimidation is starting, my friends.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:07.630
Today's example is actually an in uniform
police officer doing it.

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:09.450
This took place in Miami, Florida.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:18.110
A police officer in uniform with a Trump mask
that says Trump no more B.S. walking around

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:19.220
a polling place.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:27.150
The officer is Daniel, you Beda wearing a
Trump 20-20 mask inside a polling place at

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.539
Miami's government center.

00:00:29.539 --> 00:00:36.010
Attorney Steve Simon, who is also chairman
of the Miami Dade Democratic Party, says,

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:41.190
quote, He may have been going to vote, but
he was in full uniform with the mask and a

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.780
gun.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.690
That's voter intimidation.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:48.620
And indeed, it is illegal in the state of
Florida.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:55.070
Florida's 20-20 statutes one oh for DOT 32,
referring to political activities of state,

00:00:55.070 --> 00:01:02.530
county and municipal officers and employees,
says that no officer of the state or any county

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:08.009
or municipality can use their authority to
influence an election or to influence a vote,

00:01:08.009 --> 00:01:09.009
period.

00:01:09.009 --> 00:01:14.600
And importantly, that, quote, no employees
of the state can participate in any political

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:17.880
campaign while on duty if you violate it.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.209
It's actually a misdemeanor in the first degree.

00:01:21.209 --> 00:01:24.869
Miami police immediately alerted to it by
people who saw this.

00:01:24.869 --> 00:01:29.889
They tweeted about it saying, quote, We are
aware of the photograph being circulated of

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:33.840
a Miami police officer wearing a political
mask in uniform.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:39.740
This behavior is unacceptable, a violation
of department policy and is being addressed

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:40.740
immediately.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:43.999
Now, of course, there is a bigger issue.

00:01:43.999 --> 00:01:46.909
This is an officer who broke the law.

00:01:46.909 --> 00:01:50.249
He shouldn't be working in law enforcement,
period.

00:01:50.249 --> 00:01:53.779
But we have no national database of bad actor
police officers.

00:01:53.779 --> 00:01:54.849
We have no such requirement.

00:01:54.849 --> 00:01:56.539
We likely won't anytime soon.

00:01:56.539 --> 00:02:00.849
As I mentioned months ago, when the George
Floyd protest started in the context of the

00:02:00.849 --> 00:02:01.849
